  "title": "Redrawn Borders, Revolution and the Soviet Runtime",
  "summary": "The collapse of empires did not make identity and governance problems disappear when nation-state borders were redrawn. At the same time, the Russian Revolution established a new direction of political and economic organization, while the Soviet runtime turned revolutionary institutional design into a longer-lived state structure.",
